---
import Layout from '../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../lib/site';
const key = currentSite(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_KEY);
const agdrExample = `---
id: AgDR-0001
timestamp: 2026-02-04T12:00:00Z
agent: claude-code
model: claude-opus-4-5
trigger: user-prompt
status: executed
---

# Auth Provider for Serverless Chrome Extension

Chosen: AWS Cognito

Why: Native API Gateway integration and managed security.

Trade-off: Hosted UI limitations and AWS lock-in.`;
const orbitPlan = `PLAN REVISION 4

Outcome
Users authenticate through corporate SSO.

Acceptance
○ SSO login succeeds
○ Existing password sessions remain valid
○ Logout terminates both sessions`;
const orbitSnapshot = `PROJECT SNAPSHOT

web-app       main @ 81fee032
auth-service  main @ 4ed128ac

Current reality, captured before reconciliation.`;
const orbitReconciliation = `RECONCILIATION

✓ existing OAuth provider found
! previous auth assumption invalidated
+ one discovery deferred
→ next bounded change available`;
const interop = `{\n  \"rel\": \"implements\",\n  \"type\": \"orbit.execution-slice\",\n  \"id\": \"slice-004\"\n}`;
const orbitSlice = `EXECUTION SLICE

Configure the existing provider
for the corporate IdP.

Contributes to  AC-1
Based on       web-app @ 81fee032
               auth-service @ 4ed128ac`;
---
{key === 'agentsdlc' && <Layout><section class="page landing"><p class="pathbar">~/agentsdlc</p><p class="eyebrow">Agent SDLC</p><h1>Open artefacts for<br />agentic software engineering.</h1><p class="lede">Agents move between sessions, tools and repositories. Engineering intent and reasoning should survive them.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button quiet" href="#standards">See how Agent SDLC works ↓</a></div><div id="standards" class="standards-heading"><p class="section-label">STANDARDS</p></div><div class="standards-grid"><section class="standard editorial"><p class="section-label">STANDARD</p><p class="standard-name">ORBIT</p><h2>Keep execution aligned<br />with durable outcomes.</h2><p class="meta">Planning and Reconciliation Specification</p><p>Define intent and outcomes once. Reconcile them against current software reality. Materialise only the next bounded execution slice.</p><a href="https://orbitspec.dev">Explore ORBIT →</a><p class="meta">orbitspec.dev</p></section><section class="standard editorial"><p class="section-label">STANDARD</p><p class="standard-name">AgDR</p><h2>Record what the agent<br />decided and why.</h2><p class="meta">Agent Decision Record Specification</p><p>Preserve consequential technical decisions and rationale beyond the agent session that created the code.</p><a href="https://agdr.dev">Explore AgDR →</a><p class="meta">agdr.dev</p></section></div><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">HOW THEY WORK TOGETHER</p><h2>Independent by design.<br />Composable when useful.</h2><p class="meta">INTEROPERABILITY</p><p>ORBIT determines what work is justified next. AgDR preserves why a consequential technical decision was made during that work.</p><p>Neither standard depends on the other.</p><pre class="code">ORBIT Plan
    ↓
Reconciliation
    ↓
Execution Slice
    ↓
Agent
 ├──→ Code
 └──→ AgDR</pre><pre class="code">{interop}</pre></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">WHY AGENT SDLC</p><h2>Sessions disappear.<br />Engineering context should not.</h2><p>Agentic development creates useful context inside conversations, agent runs and prompts. Agent SDLC defines small durable artefacts for the parts that need to survive.</p></div><div class="contrast"><p><b>Transient</b><br />Conversation — useful during the session, but not a durable engineering record.<br /><br />Agent session — ends when the run finishes or context resets.<br /><br />Runtime prompt — explains what the agent knew then.</p><p><b>Durable artefacts</b><br />ORBIT Plan — preserves intended outcomes.<br /><br />AgDR — preserves why a consequential choice was made.<br /><br />Evidence can preserve what supported an assessment.<br /><br />Execution provenance can preserve what state justified work.</p></div></section><div class="trust-strip"><b>OPEN BY DEFAULT</b><span>Versioned specifications</span><span>Machine-readable schemas</span><span>Public change history</span><span>Implementation-neutral contracts</span><a href="/governance">About Agent SDLC →</a></div></section></Layout>}
{key === 'agdr' && <Layout><section class="page landing"><p class="pathbar">~/agdr</p><p class="eyebrow">AgDR 1.2.0 · OPEN STANDARD</p><h1>Record what the agent decided<br />and why.</h1><p class="lede">Your agent chose a library, a data model or an architecture. The code survived. Did the reasoning?</p><p>AgDR is a small structured Markdown record written when an AI agent makes a consequential technical decision.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/quick-start">Adopt AgDR</a><a class="button quiet" href="/specification">Read the specification</a></div><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">01 / THE RECORD</p><h2>A real decision, next to the code.</h2><pre class="code">{agdrExample}</pre><p><a href="https://github.com/me2resh/agent-decision-record/blob/main/examples/AgDR-0001-auth-provider-choice.md">View source ↗</a></p></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">02 / ADOPT</p><h2>Use AgDR with the agent you already have.</h2><div class="rows"><p><b>Claude Code</b><span>Plugin or /decide command</span></p><p><b>Codex</b><span>SKILL.md integration</span></p><p><b>Cursor</b><span>Always-on MDC rule</span></p><p><b>Copilot · Windsurf · Any AI</b><span>Repository instructions or system prompt</span></p><p><b>Git</b><span>Pre-commit and CI enforcement</span></p></div><a href="/integrations">See installation paths →</a></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">03 / THREE-FILE STANDARD</p><h2>Three files. Any agent.</h2><p>Template + schema + validator produce records in <code>docs/agdr/</code>.</p></div><pre class="code">agdr-template.md
       +
agdr.schema.json
       +
validate-agdr.js
       ↓
docs/agdr/AgDR-0001-*.md</pre></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">04 / MACHINE CHECKABLE</p><h2>A standard the agent can fail.</h2><pre class="terminal">$ node scripts/validate-agdr.js docs/agdr/*.md
✓ AgDR-0001 valid
✓ AgDR-0002 valid

2 records checked
0 errors</pre></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">05 / ADR VS AgDR</p><h2>AgDR complements ADR.</h2></div><div class="comparison"><p><b>ADR</b><br />Human architect · design process · usually manual</p><p><b>AgDR</b><br />AI agent · consequential choice · metadata and automated checks</p></div></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">06 / WHEN TO RECORD</p><h2>Record the choices that change the shape of the system.</h2><p>Libraries, architecture, migrations, data models, security and deployment choices deserve a record. Routine formatting and obvious fixes do not.</p><a href="/examples">Browse real decisions →</a></section></section></Layout>}
+{key === 'orbit' && <Layout><section class="page landing"><p class="pathbar">~/orbit</p><p class="eyebrow">ORBIT v0.1 · DRAFT</p><h1>Keep execution aligned<br />with durable outcomes.</h1><p class="lede">Plan intent once. Reconcile against reality. Materialise only the next bounded change.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/concepts">Read the model</a><a class="button quiet" href="/schemas">View schemas</a></div><div class="lifecycle"><p class="section-label">00 / THE LOOP</p>{['PLAN|Durable intent', 'OBSERVE|Current project state', 'RECONCILE|What changed?', 'SLICE|What is justified next?', 'EXECUTE|'].map((step) => { const [name,desc] = step.split('|'); return <div class="stage"><b>{name}</b><span>{desc}</span></div> })}</div><section class="split artefact-grid"><div><p class="section-label">01 / PLAN</p><pre class="code">{orbitPlan}</pre></div><div><p class="section-label">02 / PROJECT SNAPSHOT</p><pre class="code">{orbitSnapshot}</pre></div><div><p class="section-label">03 / RECONCILIATION</p><pre class="code">{orbitReconciliation}</pre></div><div><p class="section-label">04 / EXECUTION SLICE</p><pre class="code">{orbitSlice}</pre></div></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">05 / THE MODEL</p><h2>A Plan is not a backlog.</h2><p>Durable outcomes. Disposable work. ORBIT decides what change is justified next; execution systems decide how to operationalise it.</p><a href="/specification">Read the draft specification →</a></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">06 / RABBIT-HOLE PROTECTION</p><h2>A discovery does not automatically become work.</h2><p>Classify discoveries as required, supporting, adjacent or unrelated. Only knowledge required for the active outcome may become current work.</p></div><pre class="code">discovery
   │
   ▼
required for active outcome?
   ├── yes → candidate current work
   └── no  → record and defer</pre></section></section></Layout>}
